    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "Note: We assume that the difference in QTL means is $ E(z_{QQ}) - E(z_{qq}) = 2a $ and that the phenotypic distributions conditioned on the QTL genotypes have common (within-line) variance $ \\sigma_{e}^{2} $. Since $ \\sigma(x, z) $ and $ \\sigma^{2}(z) $ are unchanged by a change in the mean of z (Chapter 3), we can arbitrarily set $ E(z_{QQ}) = -E(z_{qq}) = a $. Coded this way, $ E(x) = E(z) = 0 $, simplifying calculation of $ \\sigma(x, z) $ and $ \\sigma^{2}(z) $.",
      "source_page": 454,
      "printed_page": 434,
      "source_block_ids": [
        "Genetics_chapter15:p010:b7"
      ],
      "bbox": [
        132.0,
